<h2>Seasonal campaigns that drive bookings</h2>

<p>Every auto repair shop has slow periods. January is quiet because everyone overspent in December. Mid-summer can dip because people are on holiday. The solution is not to wait for the phone to ring. It is to plan campaigns around the seasons and get ahead of the slow patches.</p>

<p>Here are the campaigns that work consistently well for auto repair shops:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Winter prep (March/April in Australia).</strong> Battery checks, tyre condition assessments, wiper blade replacements, heater and defroster inspections. Frame it as a safety check, not a sales pitch. "Is your car ready for winter?" is a message every car owner relates to.</li>
  <li><strong>Summer road trip checks (October/November).</strong> Air conditioning service, coolant levels, tyre pressure, brake inspections before long drives. Families planning road trips are already thinking about car reliability. Give them a reason to book before they leave.</li>
  <li><strong>Back-to-school car safety (late January).</strong> Parents driving kids back to school want peace of mind. Target this at families with a simple "school-run safety check" package. Tyres, brakes, lights, wipers. Bundle it at a fixed price.</li>
  <li><strong>End-of-financial-year service specials (May/June).</strong> For business owners and tradies who can claim vehicle expenses, a mid-year service timed to EOFY is a smart sell.</li>
</ul>

<p>The key with seasonal campaigns is to start them three to four weeks early. Do not send a winter prep email on the first day of winter. Send it while people are still thinking ahead. Use your customer database to target the right people. If you serviced someone's air conditioning last summer, they are your ideal audience for a cooling system check-up this year.</p>

<p>If you want to structure these campaigns as part of a broader marketing approach, our piece on <a href="/blog/sales-funnel-small-business">sales funnels for small business</a> explains how to move people from awareness through to booking.</p>

